---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Springfield Lot Striping | Commercial Striping for Greene County"
  description="Learn how Springfield Lot Striping supports commercial property managers, facility teams, and contractors with commercial parking lot striping, ADA markings, fire lanes, restriping, and warehouse line work in Springfield, MO."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-concrete">
      <h1>About Springfield Lot Striping</h1>
      <p>Springfield Lot Striping is built for commercial buyers who need clean parking layouts, readable ADA markings, fire lane striping, and reliable restriping across Springfield and Greene County. The site exists to make it easier for property managers, facility teams, and contractors to find the exact service they need without wading through general-purpose local pages that do not match commercial intent.</p>

      <p>Springfield has a broad commercial mix: retail corridors, office parks, apartment communities, medical facilities, warehouse properties, and industrial sites. Those property types do not need the same striping approach as a residential driveway or a tiny single-tenant lot. They need contractors who can work around tenant schedules, document the work clearly, and complete markings that support traffic flow, compliance, and curb appeal.</p>

      <h2>What this site helps with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Parking lot striping for new layouts and refreshed lots</li>
        <li>Commercial restriping after wear, sealcoating, or repaving</li>
        <li>ADA compliance striping and accessible stall layout updates</li>
        <li>Fire lane striping and curb markings</li>
        <li>Warehouse and industrial floor line striping</li>
        <li>Service area pages for Springfield, Nixa, Ozark, Republic, Battlefield, and Rogersville</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How requests are handled</h2>
      <p>When a visitor submits a request, the goal is to capture enough project detail to route the inquiry correctly: property type, lot size, city, timing, and the scope of work. That makes it easier for a contractor to determine whether the request is a fit, whether the work should be phased, and what documentation the buyer will need.</p>

      <p>This website is an information and lead-routing resource, not a contractor. All final scope, pricing, permits, accessibility checks, and work outcomes are handled directly by the provider that accepts the request. Property owners should always verify licensing, insurance, and written estimates before approving any work.</p>

      <h2>Why commercial-only focus matters</h2>
      <p>Commercial parking lot striping is a different market from residential paint work. Buyers care about traffic flow, stall counts, accessible spaces, overhead timing, compliance documentation, and minimizing disruption to tenants and customers. That is why this site keeps its focus on commercial lots and related industrial marking work instead of trying to cover every paint-related search in the area.</p>

      <h2>Need a quote?</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or the quote form on the homepage to start a request. Include the property city, approximate stall count, and the type of striping or compliance work needed so the request can be routed efficiently.</p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
